content.text:
The degradation traces to one fault: the `attractions` service crash-looping. Its outgoing failures reach users through the `frontend` tier.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "attractions",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND service_name='attractions' ORDER BY time", "claim": "attractions container restarts climb from 3 to 6 during the abnormal window; normal period shows 0."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.ready' AND service_name='attractions' ORDER BY time", "claim": "attractions container reports ready=0 throughout the abnormal window, versus ready=1 in the normal period."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='attractions' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "No attractions spans at all in the abnormal period, whereas the normal period has about 440 server spans."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name LIKE 'attractions.%' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend's calls to attractions fail with Error status in about 0.02 ms, failing immediately."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "attractions", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_kind IS NULL AND span_name IN ('HTTP /cinema','HTTP /museums','HTTP /restaurants') GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "User-facing frontend HTTP routes /cinema, /museums and /restaurants return 500 errors, matching the failed attractions calls."}]}
  ]
}
```

